 "_networking_basis": "Fabric API 1.20.5 replaced 1.20.4's channel networking (an Identifier plus a raw PacketByteBuf, and FabricPacket/PacketType on top of it) with CustomPayload types registered per phase and direction in PayloadTypeRegistry. compat/fapi gives 1.20.4's API back: a channel is a CbChannelPayload type of its id (impl/networking/CbChannels; registered for the receiving side when a 1.20.4 receiver is registered, the send side written through CbPayloads' fallback where nothing registered it), 1.20.4 handlers are wrapped as 1.20.5 handlers, PacketSender's dropped members dispatch to a mod's own 1.20.4 implementation (CbLegacyPacketSender) or build channel payloads for 1.20.5's senders, and a GenericFutureListener reaches its write's channel future again (CbFapiFutureListenerMixin)."
}
